The Shape class must contain:
• An abstract method double calculateArea() that calculates and returns the area.
• An abstract method double calculatePerimeter() that calculates and returns the perimeter.
• Aconcrete method displayDetails() that calls calculateArea() and calculatePerimeter() to obtain the calculated values and displays
them.
The output for each shape should be:
Shape details:
Area: <area>
Perimeter: <perimeter>
Rectangle
Create a class named Rectangle that extends Shape.
The Rectangle class must:
• Contain double variables length and width.
• Override calculateArea() using:
Area = length x width
• Override calculatePerimeter() using:
Perimeter = 2 x (length + width)
• Implement inputDetails(Scanner scanner) to read the length and width of the rectangle.
Circle
Create a class named Circle that extends Shape.
The Circle class must:
• Contain a double variable radius.
• Override calculateArea() using:
Area = Math.PI x radius x radius
• Override calculatePerimeter() using:
Perimeter = 2 x Math.PI x radius
• Implement inputDetails(Scanner scanner) to read the radius of the circle.
In the main() method:
1. Create a Scanner object.
2. Create a Rectangle object.
3. Read the rectangle's length and width using inputDetails().
4. Display the rectangle's details using displayDetails().
5. Create a Circle object.
6. Read the circle's radius using inputDetails().
7. Display the circle's details using displayDetails().
8. Close the Scanner.
Input Format:
The input consists of the following values in order:
• One double value representing the length of the rectangle.
• One double value representing the width of the rectangle.
• One double value representing the radius of the circle.
Each value is provided on a separate line.
Output Format:
Display the rectangle's details followed by the circle's details:
Shape details:
Area: <rectangle_area>
Perimeter: <rectangle_perimeter>
Shape details:
Area: <circle_area>
Perimeter: <circle_perimeter>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
abstract class Shape {
    abstract double calculateArea();
    abstract double calculatePerimeter();
 
    // Concrete method in the abstract class
    void displayDetails() {
        System.out.println("Shape details:");
        System.out.printf("Area: %.2f%n", calculateArea());
        System.out.printf("Perimeter: %.2f%n", calculatePerimeter());
    }
}
 
class Rectangle extends Shape {
    double length, width;
 
    void inputDetails(Scanner scanner) {
        length = scanner.nextDouble();
        width = scanner.nextDouble();
    }
 
    @Override
    double calculateArea() { return length * width; }
 
    @Override
    double calculatePerimeter() { return 2 * (length + width); }
}
 
class Circle extends Shape {
    double radius;
 
    void inputDetails(Scanner scanner) {
        radius = scanner.nextDouble();
    }
 
    @Override
    double calculateArea() { return Math.PI * radius * radius; }
 
    @Override
    double calculatePerimeter() { return 2 * Math.PI * radius; }
}
 
public class ShapeDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        Rectangle rect = new Rectangle();
        rect.inputDetails(scanner);
        rect.displayDetails();
        Circle circle = new Circle();
        circle.inputDetails(scanner);
        circle.displayDetails();
        scanner.close();
    }
}
